{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1167","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Bicolored RBS"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A string is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bracket sequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it does not contain any characters other than \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". A bracket sequence is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"regular"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (shortly, RBS) if it is possible to obtain correct arithmetic expression by inserting characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" into this sequence. For example, \""},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are RBS and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can see that each opening bracket in RBS is paired with some closing bracket, and, using this fact, we can define "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nesting depth"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the RBS as maximum number of bracket pairs, such that the $$$2$$$-nd pair lies inside the $$$1$$$-st one, the $$$3$$$-rd one — inside the $$$2$$$-nd one and so on. For example, nesting depth of \""},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is $$$0$$$, \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()()()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is $$$1$$$ and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()((())())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now, you are given RBS $$$s$$$ of even length $$$n$$$. You should color each bracket of $$$s$$$ into one of two colors: red or blue. Bracket sequence $$$r$$$, consisting only of red brackets, should be RBS, and bracket sequence, consisting only of blue brackets $$$b$$$, should be RBS. Any of them can be empty. You are not allowed to reorder characters in $$$s$$$, $$$r$$$ or $$$b$$$. No brackets can be left uncolored."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Among all possible variants you should choose one that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minimizes maximum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$r$$$'s and $$$b$$$'s nesting depth. If there are multiple solutions you can print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an even integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of RBS $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains regular bracket sequence $$$s$$$ ($$$|s| = n$$$, $$$s_i \\in \\{$$$\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"$$$\\}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print single string $$$t$$$ of length $$$n$$$ consisting of \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"-s and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"-s. If $$$t_i$$$ is equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" then character $$$s_i$$$ belongs to RBS $$$r$$$, otherwise $$$s_i$$$ belongs to $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n()\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n11\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n(())\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0101\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n((()())())\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0110001111"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example one of optimal solutions is $$$s = $$$ \"$$$\\color{blue}{()}$$$\". $$$r$$$ is empty and $$$b = $$$ \"$$$()$$$\". The answer is $$$\\max(0, 1) = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example it's optimal to make $$$s = $$$ \"$$$\\color{red}{(}\\color{blue}{(}\\color{red}{)}\\color{blue}{)}$$$\". $$$r = b = $$$ \"$$$()$$$\" and the answer is $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example we can make $$$s = $$$ \"$$$\\color{red}{(}\\color{blue}{((}\\color{red}{)()}\\color{blue}{)())}$$$\". $$$r = $$$ \"$$$()()$$$\" and $$$b = $$$ \"$$$(()())$$$\" and the answer is $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1167D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1167/problem/D"}